WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.750
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:11.860
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:17.430
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:26.200
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:33.950
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.420
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.290
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:44.030
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:48.690
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.370
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.370 --> 00:01:01.040
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.410
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:12.050
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:16.960
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:22.200
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:32.310
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:37.040
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:41.780
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:54.250
<i>Didn't find out about
anything today, either...</i>

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.690
<i>Not about the Blade Children,</i>

00:01:56.690 --> 00:02:02.130
<i>not about Kiyotaka-san,
not about anything at all...</i>

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:06.660
I'm home.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.060
Ayumu! I'm home!

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.130
Ayumu?

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:21.750
<i>So Little Narumi has been
released into the wild</i>

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:26.740
<i>and now wanders the nighttime
streets, still a loser...</i>

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:32.520
"The Day of Losers"

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:43.860
<i>This feeling...</i>

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.630
<i>It's like when Kiyotaka-san disappeared...</i>

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:49.460
<i>When he suddenly disappeared
without any warning...</i>

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:54.100
Ayumu?!

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:56.970
What are you yelling for?

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.310
Do you have any idea what time it is?!

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:01.880
Kids shouldn't be walking around
outside this late, you know!

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.310
It's still 9:00.

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:05.850
Not even grade school kids are asleep yet.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:09.650
Oh yeah, I'm going to stay
at a friend's place tonight.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:11.520
Have whatever you'd like for dinner.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.660
<i>And make sure you wake
up on time tomorrow.</i>

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.420
Bye.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:16.430
Wait, Ayumu!

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:20.800
You're going to come
home tomorrow...right?

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:25.330
You're not going to disappear
like Kiyotaka-san did, are you?

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:29.400
Of course not. I'm not like my brother...

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.100
Nothing like him at all...

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.910
You're acting weird!

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:35.140
What's going on?!

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:38.180
Nothing. Good night.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.150
Ayumu...

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:51.330
Ayumu resembles me so
much that I pity him.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.300
But all he does is resemble;

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.360
he will never become the same person I am.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:01.340
He may molder as he follows in my footsteps.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.140
But if he doesn't,

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:06.130
he'll probably be capable of
reaching a place I never can.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:08.310
Madoka...

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:11.650
When he stands at those crossroads,

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.270
extend a gentle hand to him.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.480
Ayumu...

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:25.890
<i>Was it...</i>

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:28.020
<i>Narumi-san, go! Hurry!</i>

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:32.100
<i>Was it right of me to run away?</i>

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:35.430
<i>Was it right of me to run
away and leave her behind?</i>

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:42.140
<i>Why...</i>

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:44.270
<i>Why am I like this?!</i>

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:50.720
Standing right there is a cowardly
loser unable to believe in himself.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:05.590
Outside the window, kira kira kira ri

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:14.200
A shooting star streaks

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:23.110
The moon, yura yura yura ri

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:31.290
naps in the ocean of stars

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.330
<i>"There are also times when the
strength to get up after a defeat</i>

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:41.230
<i>is more admirable than the
strength to never lose."</i>

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:56.720
Breakfast.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:57.720
You're late!

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.350
I'm a VIP, you know!

00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:04.290
Yeah, sure.

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:05.630
<i>Here, Hiyoko-chan!</i>

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.320
My name's Hiyono!

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.370
Bread and milk?!

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:15.040
<i>I always have Japanese-style
food in the morning!</i>

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:17.640
A breakfast without an egg,
miso soup, tofu, and seaweed

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.310
goes against common sense!

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:22.110
What does an idiot who willingly
lets herself become a hostage

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.910
know about common sense?

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:25.580
What do you mean, "idiot"?!

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:27.750
If I hadn't let you catch me back then

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:30.520
you'd be at a real disadvantage!

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:32.780
You should be thanking me.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:38.120
Aren't you scared?

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:43.400
Both me and Rio can get
rid of anyone in a snap.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:47.200
If your trump card - that tape
- finds its way to the police,

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:49.740
both she and I will
probably have hell to pay,

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:52.640
but plenty of other things have
been prepared behind the scenes.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:56.140
We could get rid of you right now.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:07:00.280
But you'd rather quietly take care
of this all if possible, right?

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:03.420
<i>As you saw, Rio-san is severely injured,</i>

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:07.960
<i>plus you all still expect
something out of Narumi-san.</i>

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:11.430
Which means you can't get
rid of me right away.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:15.730
<i>Until the rematch between Narumi-san
and Rio-san ends, I'm safe!</i>

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:17.970
I really underestimated you...

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:21.870
<i>So, have you located Narumi-san yet?</i>

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:24.940
Still can't find him...

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:30.580
It sounds like your guys' information
network isn't all that great.

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:33.250
Being able to secure such a
nearby place to confine me

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:35.250
is proof that you have a
decent amount of funds,

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:37.790
and that you have some level
of organization going on.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:41.260
But it seems there's a lack of people...

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:45.090
<i>What do you think? I tried
using logic like Narumi-san!</i>

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:51.770
I find myself thinking about
all sorts of things in here.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.940
The person who lost her memory,

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.600
the person you tried to kill,

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:59.270
the person you used to
threaten someone else,

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:02.940
and the teacher who knew too much.

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:06.080
You're in disarray.

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:09.620
It seems to me that none of you

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:13.490
have taken charge of this situation at all.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:18.290
Things are happening unbeknownst to you,

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:23.300
and you're trying to cope with that
fact before the damage reaches you.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:27.830
You're like a tiny ship in a storm.

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:32.710
<i>Narumi-san is being tossed
around by the situation too,</i>

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:36.610
but you're in trouble as well.

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:42.650
<i>Asazuki-san...</i>

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:47.350
What exactly are the Blade Children?

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.920
If you want to live long, you'll be quiet.

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:04.870
Come in!

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:08.910
You look well.

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:12.610
<i>Eyes-kun!</i>

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:22.750
I grew worried after I heard what
happened from Asazuki last night.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.330
I was worried you might be depressed,

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.760
though not nearly as
depressed as Little Narumi...

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:30.430
<i>Why would I be depressed?!</i>

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:32.800
I made him kneel to me!

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:35.900
But you lost to the Hiyono girl.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:39.960
I don't think I lost.

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:45.850
I'm just a little ashamed, that's all...

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:49.380
Because things didn't turn
out the way you expected?

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:54.160
There's that, but that's not really it.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.660
Little Narumi needs to believe in himself,

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:02.690
but we might need to believe
in him just as much, too.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:06.360
Believe?

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:10.030
In that weak younger brother
who looks only backwards?

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:12.940
<i>Say, Asazuki-san.</i>

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:15.970
What is it you're fighting?

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:22.480
<i>You need Narumi-san to win
your fight, don't you?</i>

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:26.050
<i>But not the current Narumi-san;</i>

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:30.220
you need a stronger Ayumu Narumi, huh?

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:42.700
But he's the only one who can save us.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.110
That's just what Kiyotaka said.

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:49.840
There may be no hope for us at all.

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:53.580
<i>Are you afraid, Eyes-kun?</i>

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:55.150
Afraid of being betrayed?

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:58.550
Afraid of what you
believed in falling apart?

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.420
If so...

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:04.590
...then you're the same as Little
Narumi, who gave up believing

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:07.530
to avoid being hurt any more!

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:15.670
I don't do wearisome
things like fight hard.

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:18.570
Plus I don't think that
highly of that bastard.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:24.950
<i>I don't care if I'm not saved.</i>

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.680
<i>I committed murders of my own free will,</i>

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:31.490
<i>and I became a criminal of my own free will.</i>

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:34.290
<i>I don't expect to be forgiven.</i>

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:38.280
<i>When the time for redemption comes,
I'll look forward and greet it.</i>

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:45.300
I don't really know much about you guys,

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:47.240
but I don't think you can ever be happy

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:49.140
unless you fight fate!

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:53.910
Would anyone ever fight a battle
they knew they would lose?

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:55.640
They'd have to be stupid...

00:11:57.710 --> 00:11:59.410
<i>Really stupid...</i>

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:02.850
Because Little Narumi
couldn't believe in himself,

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:04.890
he wound up yielding to me.

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:07.760
<i>And since Hiyono-san believed in him,</i>

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.590
she got the best of me.

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:13.190
I was taught a lesson once again.

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:16.760
Only believers will always be happy...

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:18.830
Rio...

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:22.400
Are you going to face off
with Little Narumi again?

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.170
I'm not really sure.

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:28.240
I don't know if he can make a comeback,

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:31.310
and I don't know what kind
of fighting he's capable of...

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:33.110
But...

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:36.020
But if he comes at me, I'll
meet him with full force!

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:39.690
This time I'll come out swinging!

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:46.890
Sad as it is, that's the
only way to change our fate...

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:50.090
<i>Fate...</i>

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:53.300
Rio.

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:56.630
Even though we're cursed,
we're still friends.

00:12:57.370 --> 00:12:59.140
I don't want you to die.

00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:01.170
Take care of yourself.

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:03.640
<i>Eyes-kun!</i>

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:08.570
Thanks for the melon...

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:18.420
<i>Even if the time comes for
our soul-burning redemption...</i>

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:29.340
The investigations aren't
making any progress at all...

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:32.210
The teacher's murder, the bomb incident...

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:34.580
We can't figure out a
clear motive for either.

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:37.010
We checked into how the two may be related

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:39.280
but we found no real connection.

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:42.680
The only certainty is
that your brother-in-law

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:46.290
was involved in both incidents, as usual.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:47.220
Yes...

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:53.060
<i>Ayumu is trying to follow the
same path as Kiyotaka-san...</i>

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:58.000
<i>The same path as Kiyotaka-san,
who disappeared</i>

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:01.970
<i>after announcing his pursuit of
the mystery of the Blade Children...</i>

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:05.800
"He may molder as he
follows in my footsteps."

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:10.210
"I'm not like my brother..."

00:14:10.210 --> 00:14:12.380
<i>Even though he's traveling the same path,</i>

00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:16.410
<i>Kiyotaka-san's shadow may
be trying to crush him...</i>

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:20.320
"I'm not like my brother..."

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:22.160
"But if he doesn't,

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:25.150
he'll probably be capable of
reaching a place I never can."

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:29.360
"When he stands at those crossroads..."

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:34.690
Assistant Inspector?
Where are you going?!

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:52.280
Madoka...

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:56.010
Leave me alone!

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:02.520
It's you...

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:04.230
Yeah.

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:06.630
<i>Nice to meet you, Ayumu-kun!</i>

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:20.840
<i>Ayumu...</i>

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:32.760
<i>Where in the world are you?</i>

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:44.160
<i>Ayumu!</i>

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:28.810
Fate can't be changed.

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:32.040
Are you so sure?

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:54.210
Come to think of it,

00:16:54.210 --> 00:16:56.280
this is where we first met, huh?

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.640
Madoka?!

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:02.950
Do you remember that day?

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:07.390
You told me that fate can't be changed...

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:12.630
This is the first time I've
seen you look like that.

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:16.300
I'm usually the one who's
depressed and looking down.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:18.290
I'm not depressed.

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:25.040
<i>You're the spitting
image of Kiyotaka-san.</i>

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:28.880
I already told you,
I'm not like my brother!

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:29.910
No.

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:32.710
<i>You've always chased after Kiyotaka-san</i>

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:34.820
ever since you were little.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:37.320
But you've grown angry at yourself

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.990
for never catching up to him.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.890
I couldn't care less about that!

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:42.990
If you couldn't care less

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:46.090
then you wouldn't get so emotional about it.

00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:49.790
And start looking at people
when you talk to them!

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:57.840
What does it matter if
you can't be his equal?

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:00.740
That doesn't mean your life's over.

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:04.670
You wouldn't understand!

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:07.950
My brother stole everything from me!

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:09.950
If I don't win, I can't take it back!

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:11.850
If I don't win, my life is...

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:13.410
You know...

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:22.500
No matter how you're feeling,
I'll always be by your side...

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:26.560
Just because you lost doesn't
mean you'll lose everything.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:31.210
You wouldn't understand!

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:33.140
If I lose, I lose everything!

00:18:33.140 --> 00:18:35.640
I can't protect what's important to me!

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:37.810
If that's what you believe...

00:18:37.810 --> 00:18:40.580
...then you shouldn't be here,
acting depressed.

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:49.790
It's okay if you come home
crying once in a while...

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:53.130
If you stay like this
you'll never win anything.

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:55.060
Anyway, regardless of
whether you win or lose,

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:57.700
I really need you around the house!

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:01.100
<i>You're in charge of the kitchen
work and laundry, after all.</i>

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:02.090
Got that?

00:19:11.810 --> 00:19:13.070
<i>Kiyotaka-san...</i>

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:16.280
"When he stands at those crossroads,

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:18.650
extend a gentle hand to him."

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:22.950
<i>Was that how you wanted?</i>

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:35.970
Rain? It was just sunny a while ago...

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:38.640
They said scattered thunderstorms...

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:41.870
Oh man, I hate thunder...

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:48.650
<i>Urgh! Kosuke-kun!</i>

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:51.250
These Puzzle Rings won't come undone at all!

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:53.780
There'd be no point if
they came undone easily.

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:57.150
I'll undo you!

00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:00.150
<i>Geez...</i>

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:03.030
<i>She's so childish...</i>

00:20:05.030 --> 00:20:07.200
I can't get them undone at all!

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:08.290
Hey, now...

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:18.480
<i>There's no reason to be
that scared of thunder, Rio...</i>

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:19.970
But!

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:24.650
Little Narumi?!

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:30.990
You're supposed to knock before
you enter a girl's room, you know.

00:20:30.990 --> 00:20:33.760
You probably didn't hear
because of the thunder.

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:38.330
So what do you want,
Mr. Dripping-Wet Loser?

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:40.820
Even losers have pride.

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:52.940
Let's make a trade.

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:11.370
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:18.070
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:36.220
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:36.220 --> 00:21:41.860
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:47.770
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:54.340
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.340 --> 00:22:00.080
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:05.290
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:11.130
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:11.130 --> 00:22:22.740
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:22.740 --> 00:22:28.510
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.510 --> 00:22:34.810
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:39.340 --> 00:22:41.770
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:44.880
Life, with its ups and downs!

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:45.950
Labor done in vain!

00:22:45.950 --> 00:22:47.880
Prayer for divine aid!

00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:51.720
<i>Next episode's highlight is
Hiyono-chan's solo train excursion!</i>

00:22:51.720 --> 00:22:53.890
All aboard the non-stop train!

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:55.090
"At each train station,

00:22:55.090 --> 00:22:56.390
none of the fast express trains

00:22:56.390 --> 00:22:57.630
will ever make stops..."

00:22:57.630 --> 00:22:59.560
A haiku by Hiyo Hiyo.

00:22:59.560 --> 00:23:01.860
On the next Spiral: Bond of Reasoning...

00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:03.330
All That You Can Do

00:23:03.330 --> 00:23:04.500
Be sure to watch it!

00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:06.630
That's all for today's Hiyono's Playhouse!
